1
00:00:52,595 --> 00:00:53,429
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:54,430
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:55,389
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:56,348
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,144
Why would you go that far for me?

6
00:01:01,562 --> 00:01:03,147
What do you want from me?

7
00:01:04,899 --> 00:01:06,233
One thing is for sure.

8
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,445
It's not because of the settlement.

9
00:01:38,474 --> 00:01:39,475
Wait, Namgung.

10
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:41,811
I'll explain everything.

11
00:01:46,273 --> 00:01:47,942
Will you let go of my arm?

12
00:02:01,372 --> 00:02:02,248
Explain?

13
00:02:03,791 --> 00:02:05,167
Explain what?

14
00:02:08,671 --> 00:02:10,256
You said nothing happened.

15
00:02:11,549 --> 00:02:13,425
That I had nothing to worry about.

16
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:17,221
Hey, Lee Mi-do.

17
00:02:27,398 --> 00:02:30,025
I was completely out of my mind that day.

18
00:02:32,236 --> 00:02:36,073
I didn't mean a single word I said.

19
00:02:36,866 --> 00:02:40,452
I was just so drunk that day,

20
00:02:40,578 --> 00:02:41,996
and I wasn't thinking straight--

21
00:02:42,121 --> 00:02:43,664
Will you just shut up?

22
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:46,792
I really don't want to hear it.

23
00:02:54,967 --> 00:02:55,885
I'm sorry.

24
00:03:55,486 --> 00:04:01,367
7. ARE WE ALLIES OR ENEMIES?

25
00:04:04,495 --> 00:04:06,288
HANGYEOL CHILDREN'S HOME

26
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:07,373
Yes, Chairman.

27
00:04:07,498 --> 00:04:09,792
I heard Seong-hyeon won first place again.

28
00:04:09,917 --> 00:04:11,460
Congratulations.

29
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:16,632
Oh, I'll make sure
to keep Tae-seung in line.

30
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:19,051
I talked to Reporter Ko,

31
00:04:19,176 --> 00:04:20,970
so you don't need to worry.

32
00:04:21,095 --> 00:04:23,722
Yes, I'll be in touch.

33
00:04:34,817 --> 00:04:35,651
Tae-seung.

34
00:04:36,902 --> 00:04:38,612
What did I always tell you?

35
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:41,115
You must share and be generous.

36
00:04:43,534 --> 00:04:44,952
That makes you a good boy.

37
00:04:46,495 --> 00:04:47,538
No.

38
00:04:48,789 --> 00:04:49,748
I won't do it.

39
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:53,711
I'll tip off another reporter.

40
00:04:54,378 --> 00:04:55,337
No.

41
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,966
I'll go to the news stations.

42
00:04:59,091 --> 00:05:01,510
I will never again

43
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:04,013
take tests

44
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:07,474
for someone else.

45
00:05:56,023 --> 00:05:57,024
Mr. Han Tae-seung.

46
00:06:12,164 --> 00:06:14,875
This is Kim Jeong-hwan
from Line Intercontinental.

47
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:16,710
You really don't know him?

48
00:06:25,677 --> 00:06:27,513
INCOMING CALL

49
00:06:30,182 --> 00:06:32,142
Is this Attorney Han Tae-seung?

50
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:33,102
Who is this?

51
00:06:33,227 --> 00:06:35,938
I'm Kim Jeong-hwan
from Line Intercontinental.

52
00:06:36,522 --> 00:06:38,107
I'm calling with a tip.

53
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:43,112
You're really trying
to screw up your life for a few bucks.

54
00:06:53,122 --> 00:06:55,082
Take the cash and go to that address.

55
00:06:55,207 --> 00:06:57,960
Don't answer anyone until I contact you.

56
00:07:00,796 --> 00:07:02,422
Not doing this for me.

57
00:07:03,882 --> 00:07:05,259
I'm doing it for you.

58
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:10,222
If you want to live and keep this money,
do exactly as I say.

59
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:16,603
Oh, I thought it was a prank call.

60
00:07:18,647 --> 00:07:21,108
I guess he really was a researcher.

61
00:07:24,111 --> 00:07:26,488
This is Kim Jeong-hwan's
last known location.

62
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:29,324
Coincidentally, it's an alley
near Jaekang Law Firm.

63
00:07:30,325 --> 00:07:32,953
Can you confirm
where you were at this time?

64
00:07:33,662 --> 00:07:35,164
The day of Seoul's first snow.

65
00:07:36,582 --> 00:07:38,125
The first snow…

66
00:07:40,002 --> 00:07:42,421
Since Jaekang Law Firm's security
was hacked that day,

67
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:44,339
we couldn't check security cameras.

68
00:07:46,592 --> 00:07:49,845
Can anyone verify your whereabouts
after 10:00?

69
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:04,526
No, there isn't anyone.

70
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:08,530
Did you really not see

71
00:08:09,573 --> 00:08:10,866
Researcher Kim Jeong-hwan?

72
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:13,702
He walked right in, and you missed him?

73
00:08:14,578 --> 00:08:17,414
That was before I knew
he ran off with internal data.

74
00:08:18,624 --> 00:08:21,835
I figured Line was playing dirty tricks
before the trial,

75
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:23,420
so I ignored it.

76
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:31,803
No matter what happens,

77
00:08:31,929 --> 00:08:35,057
we must find Kim Jeong-hwan's data
before Jisang does.

78
00:08:36,016 --> 00:08:37,100
Don't worry.

79
00:08:37,809 --> 00:08:39,686
I'm looking into every connection,

80
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:43,315
even tracking down his first love.

81
00:08:48,654 --> 00:08:51,740
Oh, and don't worry about the police.

82
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:53,450
The higher-ups will sort it.

83
00:08:59,248 --> 00:09:00,165
Hey, Attorney Lee.

84
00:09:05,963 --> 00:09:07,923
What's taking so long?

85
00:09:09,466 --> 00:09:10,300
What?

86
00:09:12,636 --> 00:09:13,762
An hour?

87
00:09:17,641 --> 00:09:19,059
The living room console.

88
00:09:19,935 --> 00:09:22,104
There's a silver safe inside it.

89
00:09:24,439 --> 00:09:28,193
But what you're looking for
won't be in there.

90
00:09:34,074 --> 00:09:35,033
You heard him?

91
00:09:36,451 --> 00:09:37,452
Bring it here now.

92
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,336
How long have you known?

93
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:50,924
I found out on the third

94
00:09:51,049 --> 00:09:53,093
that Line Intercontinental
was raided by the FSS.

95
00:09:53,677 --> 00:09:56,722
I didn't know anything about
the Malaysian account until yesterday.

96
00:09:56,847 --> 00:10:01,101
And I learned that Director Bang from Line
deposited money into it…

97
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,521
just 45 minutes ago.

98
00:10:07,399 --> 00:10:10,485
Things got complicated
with Line's succession issue.

99
00:10:11,069 --> 00:10:12,529
It's going to get worse

100
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:14,698
if Assemblyman Shin's
airport project fails.

101
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:16,867
It'll be settled out of court.

102
00:10:17,784 --> 00:10:21,079
See it as taking a few years off
and cooperate with their investigation.

103
00:10:25,584 --> 00:10:26,835
What if I refuse?

104
00:10:31,882 --> 00:10:33,216
You must have…

105
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:36,636
Kim Jeong-hwan's data.

106
00:10:36,762 --> 00:10:37,637
Please.

107
00:10:39,389 --> 00:10:40,932
You think that's all I have?

108
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:45,354
I've worked under you for five years.

109
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:52,903
You have one week.

110
00:10:54,488 --> 00:10:56,740
Handle my police investigation first.

111
00:10:58,075 --> 00:11:01,119
Otherwise, your father-in-law

112
00:11:01,244 --> 00:11:03,038
will be the first to be investigated.

113
00:11:12,214 --> 00:11:13,256
Did those two fight?

114
00:11:13,382 --> 00:11:16,259
Still, why would he ghost us
for days like this?

115
00:11:18,887 --> 00:11:19,805
Namgung!

116
00:11:21,098 --> 00:11:22,182
You in there?

117
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:34,444
Lee Mi-do.

118
00:11:35,195 --> 00:11:36,113
What?

119
00:11:39,074 --> 00:11:39,908
Mi-do.

120
00:11:58,468 --> 00:12:00,429
CHAT

121
00:12:00,554 --> 00:12:01,721
YEONG-DO

122
00:12:01,847 --> 00:12:03,432
Namgung, good job.

123
00:12:03,557 --> 00:12:04,975
Whatever's going on,

124
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:07,602
Lee Mi-do looks completely wrecked
and is really sorry.

125
00:12:09,438 --> 00:12:12,357
Anyway, Namgung,
do we pick up Mom's blood pressure meds

126
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:14,901
this Friday or next week?

127
00:12:16,361 --> 00:12:18,029
Nothing's wrong, right?

128
00:12:18,155 --> 00:12:19,990
Where are you staying right now?

129
00:12:21,408 --> 00:12:24,536
The card reader broke again.
Got the repair center number?

130
00:12:24,661 --> 00:12:27,706
MIDORI

131
00:13:11,791 --> 00:13:13,376
Come back home.

132
00:13:13,502 --> 00:13:14,878
I'll move out.

133
00:13:15,462 --> 00:13:17,714
You can't sleep well anywhere else.

134
00:13:19,382 --> 00:13:20,550
Let me ask you this.

135
00:13:23,845 --> 00:13:25,931
Did you only direct films because of me?

136
00:13:31,353 --> 00:13:33,021
It's not like that, Namgung.

137
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:35,148
It's not.

138
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:38,235
Then what was that bastard saying?

139
00:13:39,861 --> 00:13:43,740
He said you wanted to run away
but you were too ashamed to tell me.

140
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:49,079
I was just so exhausted.
I said it in the heat of the moment.

141
00:13:51,873 --> 00:13:55,168
Honestly, I should've just given up
after failing so much.

142
00:13:56,795 --> 00:13:58,129
But that was too hard.

143
00:13:59,297 --> 00:14:01,299
So I used you as an excuse.

144
00:14:03,677 --> 00:14:05,011
Actually, Namgung…

145
00:14:06,096 --> 00:14:08,932
I realized something
while shooting this film.

146
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:13,311
My skills…

147
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:16,314
are completely pathetic.

148
00:14:18,275 --> 00:14:21,736
I don't have what it takes
to shoot a film of this scale.

149
00:14:22,571 --> 00:14:23,822
I'm not lying.

150
00:14:24,864 --> 00:14:26,032
I mean it.

151
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:30,620
I'm not as good a director
as you think I am.

152
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:34,207
It's not because of bad luck
or a lack of opportunity.

153
00:14:36,084 --> 00:14:37,586
I just have no talent.

154
00:14:45,343 --> 00:14:46,928
I'm terrible, aren't I?

155
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:49,889
You must be disappointed.

156
00:14:50,557 --> 00:14:52,475
You're a real piece of work.

157
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:56,438
Why are you telling me this now?

158
00:14:57,105 --> 00:15:00,692
You think I don't know you want me
to let this slide out of pity?

159
00:15:00,817 --> 00:15:01,943
Why?

160
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:03,945
Am I some dumb sucker

161
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:07,073
who thinks the world is ending
if you're hurting?

162
00:15:07,699 --> 00:15:09,159
You're using me right now.

163
00:15:09,951 --> 00:15:11,411
You're using your pain against me

164
00:15:11,536 --> 00:15:14,164
because you know I'm weak
when it comes to you. Right?

165
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:18,460
Yeah, you're right.

166
00:15:20,128 --> 00:15:21,129
I'm using you.

167
00:15:22,213 --> 00:15:24,007
So please, for just one more time,

168
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:27,927
can you look the other way?

169
00:15:36,394 --> 00:15:37,395
No, I can't.

170
00:15:39,272 --> 00:15:40,440
I've thought about it

171
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:43,652
a hundred times over,
but I can't look at you the same way.

172
00:15:49,032 --> 00:15:50,867
We need to rethink getting married.

173
00:15:53,912 --> 00:15:55,330
If you're done, please leave.

174
00:16:08,927 --> 00:16:11,596
Don't get too used to this place.

175
00:16:13,181 --> 00:16:15,183
It's only until your stitches come out.

176
00:16:21,231 --> 00:16:23,316
Don't give me that cute look.

177
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:28,655
You're a living thing,
so I'd have to take care of you for life.

178
00:16:28,780 --> 00:16:30,448
And I honestly can't handle that.

179
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:34,661
But I'm looking for someone good
to adopt you, so just wait.

180
00:16:40,375 --> 00:16:43,169
I have the perfect person in mind, though.

181
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:49,426
Bambi, it's someone you know too.

182
00:16:49,551 --> 00:16:52,303
He has some cat dad experience.

183
00:16:52,429 --> 00:16:55,932
And you'd prefer someone you know
over a total stranger, right?

184
00:16:57,308 --> 00:17:00,562
I sent him your picture
and asked him, just in case.

185
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:06,818
But he didn't reply after reading it.

186
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:14,242
Bambi, let me show you. Look.

187
00:17:16,119 --> 00:17:20,290
Hey, even you think
this is a bit much, right?

188
00:17:21,583 --> 00:17:24,753
Sure, he's been going through
a rough patch lately.

189
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:30,133
But still, I clearly sent this message
because I was worried about him.

190
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:33,178
Leaving me on read is just too mean.

191
00:17:33,928 --> 00:17:35,722
Look, I wrote this long text.

192
00:17:35,847 --> 00:17:37,807
And you're so cute!

193
00:17:43,146 --> 00:17:44,564
Yeah, okay.

194
00:17:45,190 --> 00:17:47,275
I guess he can leave me on read.

195
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,485
Yeah.

196
00:17:48,610 --> 00:17:49,944
Who am I, anyway?

197
00:17:54,407 --> 00:17:55,325
TF TEAM 3
NAMGUNG HO

198
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,326
Huh?

199
00:17:57,452 --> 00:17:58,703
Why is this…

200
00:18:05,084 --> 00:18:07,420
Wh-- Why is this here?

201
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:38,159
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

202
00:18:40,662 --> 00:18:42,872
I tweaked the sugar like you asked.

203
00:18:43,623 --> 00:18:46,751
Surface moisture is 0.8 lower
than the fourth batch.

204
00:18:48,586 --> 00:18:50,713
I let it cool, so it won't be hot.

205
00:18:53,466 --> 00:18:54,509
Mr. Namgung?

206
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:56,553
Mr. Namgung!

207
00:18:57,136 --> 00:18:58,388
Oh, right.

208
00:19:14,779 --> 00:19:16,281
We followed the recipe.

209
00:19:16,406 --> 00:19:17,866
Weird aftertaste, right?

210
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,201
These sweet potatoes…

211
00:19:20,326 --> 00:19:23,121
I usually get a small batch from the farm.

212
00:19:23,246 --> 00:19:27,125
But I had to go to the Cheonan Factory,
so I grabbed a few from there.

213
00:19:27,250 --> 00:19:30,086
The Factory Manager found out later
and threw a huge fit.

214
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,589
Any sweet potatoes left?

215
00:19:32,714 --> 00:19:34,507
You couldn't have used them all.

216
00:19:35,216 --> 00:19:37,427
Mr. Namgung took them this morning.

217
00:19:38,386 --> 00:19:39,220
What?

218
00:19:43,683 --> 00:19:45,727
The left side is slippery.

219
00:19:48,104 --> 00:19:50,607
You knew when you took them, right?

220
00:19:50,732 --> 00:19:52,358
Where are the sweet potatoes?

221
00:19:53,234 --> 00:19:55,278
Why should I tell you that?

222
00:19:56,988 --> 00:19:58,865
Those are definitely imported.

223
00:19:58,990 --> 00:20:01,075
Imports have different pesticide levels.

224
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,578
Testing them will give us solid evidence.

225
00:20:04,662 --> 00:20:06,831
You've heard of
the Bread Pie Mass Rebate Incident,

226
00:20:08,249 --> 00:20:09,083
haven't you?

227
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:10,668
Yes.

228
00:20:11,461 --> 00:20:12,795
It's a famous case.

229
00:20:12,921 --> 00:20:14,672
Manager Eom was on that team.

230
00:20:15,882 --> 00:20:18,301
People think they were fired
after being audited,

231
00:20:18,426 --> 00:20:20,803
but that wasn't the case.
They were demoted, not fired.

232
00:20:20,929 --> 00:20:22,764
To be exact, it was retaliation.

233
00:20:22,889 --> 00:20:24,599
They were going to blow the whistle.

234
00:20:26,517 --> 00:20:28,853
Except for Manager Eom,
the rest of the team

235
00:20:29,896 --> 00:20:31,981
all quit within a year.

236
00:20:32,982 --> 00:20:34,651
He couldn't afford to quit.

237
00:20:36,653 --> 00:20:38,279
His oldest plays the piano.

238
00:20:39,739 --> 00:20:41,616
And she was way too good at it.

239
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:51,793
At best, a department transfer.

240
00:20:51,918 --> 00:20:54,504
At worst, a demotion
and a transfer to a rural plant.

241
00:20:54,629 --> 00:20:57,298
And you're shunned by the team
and denied promotions.

242
00:20:57,423 --> 00:20:59,133
Who could endure that?

243
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:00,802
Manager Eom said

244
00:21:01,386 --> 00:21:03,721
he'd have quit
if his daughter was just smart.

245
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:07,684
But unfortunately, she's a total genius.

246
00:21:08,893 --> 00:21:11,020
I know you're just trying to scare me.

247
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:13,272
I forgot the most important part.

248
00:21:13,398 --> 00:21:15,900
They even dug up his family history.

249
00:21:18,069 --> 00:21:21,948
His wife was the victim of a crime,
severe enough to make the news.

250
00:21:23,950 --> 00:21:25,994
And they posted about it
on the company intranet.

251
00:21:38,131 --> 00:21:41,009
This might be harder than you think.

252
00:21:44,387 --> 00:21:45,680
I'm prepared for that.

253
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:48,474
You're holding up well, too.

254
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:50,560
I can do the same.

255
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:55,106
I haven't been holding up well.

256
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,943
I'm actually really struggling.

257
00:22:02,196 --> 00:22:03,406
Like, a whole lot.

258
00:22:08,119 --> 00:22:10,121
-Have a good night.
-You too.

259
00:22:12,665 --> 00:22:15,626
Su-a. Your report got rejected again.

260
00:22:15,752 --> 00:22:18,087
-Let's just head out.
-I'll stay a bit longer.

261
00:22:18,212 --> 00:22:19,464
You can go ahead.

262
00:22:20,006 --> 00:22:21,132
Oh, really? Okay.

263
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:23,551
Well, actually…

264
00:22:23,676 --> 00:22:27,013
I was going to suggest
we go cheer up Assistant Manager Gung.

265
00:22:48,076 --> 00:22:49,160
Careful.

266
00:22:49,285 --> 00:22:50,495
Wow, this is…

267
00:22:52,288 --> 00:22:53,164
Oh, boy.

268
00:22:59,879 --> 00:23:01,297
Oh, Mr. Namgung…

269
00:23:01,839 --> 00:23:03,758
He must be having a really hard time.

270
00:23:05,176 --> 00:23:06,260
Hello?

271
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:07,220
Is this the driver?

272
00:23:07,887 --> 00:23:08,805
No.

273
00:23:08,930 --> 00:23:11,265
We're at Exit 4, not Exit 3.

274
00:23:12,225 --> 00:23:14,268
It's on the opposite side.

275
00:23:15,019 --> 00:23:16,729
No, not Exit 3. It's…

276
00:23:34,205 --> 00:23:35,498
Mr. Namgung.

277
00:23:35,623 --> 00:23:37,458
Are you really drunk?

278
00:23:42,213 --> 00:23:43,172
What you said

279
00:23:44,215 --> 00:23:47,093
was a lie, right? To make me give up.

280
00:23:52,974 --> 00:23:54,433
Is this an act too?

281
00:23:55,226 --> 00:23:57,436
One bottle of soju
can't make you this drunk.

282
00:24:00,690 --> 00:24:02,275
Are you really drunk?

283
00:24:09,490 --> 00:24:10,867
Then…

284
00:24:11,534 --> 00:24:13,035
since you're drunk…

285
00:24:15,037 --> 00:24:16,789
can I tell you something?

286
00:24:19,041 --> 00:24:21,169
Because I might never get another chance.

287
00:24:29,177 --> 00:24:30,636
Mr. Namgung, I…

288
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:34,807
I li…

289
00:24:37,602 --> 00:24:38,561
I like…

290
00:24:43,608 --> 00:24:45,359
Where are the sweet potatoes?

291
00:24:46,569 --> 00:24:49,780
You didn't throw them away, right?
You didn't, did you?

292
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,201
I threw them away.

293
00:24:53,326 --> 00:24:55,119
What? You did?

294
00:24:59,707 --> 00:25:02,793
Where? Where did you throw them?

295
00:25:03,836 --> 00:25:06,047
Route 6.

296
00:25:06,172 --> 00:25:07,048
What?

297
00:25:09,133 --> 00:25:11,052
Route 6.

298
00:25:11,177 --> 00:25:13,512
Route 6? Route 6.

299
00:25:15,181 --> 00:25:17,141
Coming from Incheon Research Center
to Seoul?

300
00:25:17,266 --> 00:25:19,310
"Keep your 20-year-old joints…

301
00:25:20,978 --> 00:25:24,523
healthy until you're 80. Knee slap!"

302
00:25:25,566 --> 00:25:26,692
"Knee slap"?

303
00:25:26,817 --> 00:25:27,777
What?

304
00:25:28,653 --> 00:25:35,034
"Keep your 20-year-old joints healthy
until you're 80. Knee slap!"

305
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:37,703
"Keep your 20-year-old joints
healthy until you're 80"?

306
00:25:37,828 --> 00:25:38,871
Knee slap…

307
00:25:38,996 --> 00:25:40,081
Knee slap!

308
00:25:40,498 --> 00:25:41,332
That's it.

309
00:25:41,457 --> 00:25:45,002
By the Dongbo Pharma billboard.
There's a field and a ditch.

310
00:25:45,127 --> 00:25:46,003
Right?

311
00:25:46,587 --> 00:25:48,923
You dumped them there, right?

312
00:26:14,949 --> 00:26:16,033
Mi-do.

313
00:26:21,038 --> 00:26:22,915
Lee Mi-do.

314
00:26:46,522 --> 00:26:48,065
Is she a no-show again?

315
00:26:51,944 --> 00:26:55,406
Did she really quit directing or what?

316
00:26:56,032 --> 00:26:58,826
Ugh, why can't I see inside?

317
00:27:30,274 --> 00:27:31,108
Hey, Han.

318
00:27:31,233 --> 00:27:32,693
You're late.

319
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:34,070
We started without you.

320
00:27:44,538 --> 00:27:46,248
What's going on here?

321
00:27:46,832 --> 00:27:48,209
What does it look like?

322
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:51,796
I made a special plea to Director Lee.

323
00:27:52,338 --> 00:27:55,091
I asked her
to help you out just this once.

324
00:27:57,468 --> 00:27:58,761
Have a seat.

325
00:28:05,851 --> 00:28:07,353
It seems Han hid it

326
00:28:07,478 --> 00:28:10,022
because he was afraid
of causing you trouble.

327
00:28:10,147 --> 00:28:11,982
He's in a tough spot right now.

328
00:28:12,733 --> 00:28:15,694
We desperately need your testimony.

329
00:28:18,489 --> 00:28:21,117
You two must have a lot to talk about.

330
00:28:21,242 --> 00:28:23,077
I'll be on my way now.

331
00:28:24,745 --> 00:28:26,122
I have a big trial.

332
00:28:43,639 --> 00:28:46,058
I don't know what Seo told you, but…

333
00:28:46,183 --> 00:28:47,226
I'm not testifying.

334
00:28:48,644 --> 00:28:50,688
I don't buy everything he says,

335
00:28:50,813 --> 00:28:53,399
but I don't want to be
involved with you anymore.

336
00:28:55,276 --> 00:28:57,903
I wouldn't have come
if I had known you were coming.

337
00:28:58,779 --> 00:28:59,738
I'm leaving.

338
00:29:13,836 --> 00:29:16,547
If you don't testify,
my career as a lawyer is over.

339
00:29:17,381 --> 00:29:18,507
Still won't do it?

340
00:29:20,301 --> 00:29:22,261
You're very capable, Han Tae-seung.

341
00:29:23,137 --> 00:29:25,139
I'm sure there are other solutions.

342
00:29:25,264 --> 00:29:26,223
You'll find one.

343
00:29:26,348 --> 00:29:27,641
No, there isn't.

344
00:29:28,184 --> 00:29:30,478
If you don't testify,
my whole life is screwed.

345
00:29:30,603 --> 00:29:32,062
You really won't do it?

346
00:29:37,193 --> 00:29:38,235
No.

347
00:29:45,284 --> 00:29:46,243
That's harsh.

348
00:29:47,036 --> 00:29:48,913
I'm not being harsh.

349
00:29:49,663 --> 00:29:52,750
You fell into this trap
because you work for a guy like him.

350
00:29:53,918 --> 00:29:56,462
Just grit your teeth and get through it.

351
00:29:57,004 --> 00:29:58,047
You're so capable.

352
00:29:59,006 --> 00:29:59,882
A trap?

353
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:07,389
A trap.

354
00:30:08,182 --> 00:30:09,808
Who said it was a trap?

355
00:30:14,980 --> 00:30:16,440
That trial…

356
00:30:18,526 --> 00:30:19,818
I lost it on purpose.

357
00:30:23,614 --> 00:30:25,157
And that whistleblower?

358
00:30:26,075 --> 00:30:27,743
I did meet him that day.

359
00:30:30,704 --> 00:30:32,498
I don't buy it. That day--

360
00:30:32,623 --> 00:30:34,333
While you were sleeping,

361
00:30:34,458 --> 00:30:40,297
going there and handling it
took less than ten minutes.

362
00:30:41,423 --> 00:30:43,008
I work pretty fast.

363
00:30:48,180 --> 00:30:49,098
Director Lee.

364
00:30:52,017 --> 00:30:54,019
Keep treating me like this.

365
00:30:54,687 --> 00:30:56,855
Keep completely ignoring me like this.

366
00:30:59,567 --> 00:31:01,735
If I lose my mind and call, don't answer.

367
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:03,028
Even if I show up…

368
00:31:06,574 --> 00:31:07,741
ignore me completely.

369
00:31:10,202 --> 00:31:11,787
Same goes for Seo Ju-hyeok.

370
00:31:14,290 --> 00:31:17,876
This better be the last time you come
running like a fool when he calls.

371
00:31:18,586 --> 00:31:19,587
Otherwise…

372
00:31:23,173 --> 00:31:25,551
your life will be completely ruined.

373
00:31:41,817 --> 00:31:45,029
What happened?
You said you wiped the video and logs!

374
00:31:45,154 --> 00:31:46,322
Yeah, I wiped them.

375
00:31:46,447 --> 00:31:48,824
Then how does Seo Ju-hyeok know Mi-do?

376
00:31:48,949 --> 00:31:51,035
How does he know about that day?

377
00:31:51,160 --> 00:31:53,787
Oh, because I gave them to him.

378
00:31:54,872 --> 00:31:58,626
Sorry, Seo's offer
was too good to turn down.

379
00:31:58,751 --> 00:32:00,878
But I didn't give up the whistleblower.

380
00:32:01,003 --> 00:32:03,672
That's my final act of loyalty
after three years.

381
00:32:03,797 --> 00:32:05,257
Best of luck to you.

382
00:32:33,744 --> 00:32:35,204
Was all of that true?

383
00:32:38,290 --> 00:32:40,542
Answer me. Is it true?

384
00:33:02,523 --> 00:33:04,149
You deliberately lost the trial

385
00:33:04,274 --> 00:33:08,862
and put that so-called whistleblower
up to it?

386
00:33:09,571 --> 00:33:12,449
Why? Are you going to run to the cops?

387
00:33:12,574 --> 00:33:13,867
Answer me.

388
00:33:14,493 --> 00:33:15,327
Did you?

389
00:33:15,452 --> 00:33:16,453
Yeah.

390
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:18,372
I did. So what?

391
00:33:20,082 --> 00:33:21,750
Didn't you know I'm trash?

392
00:33:21,875 --> 00:33:23,001
Yes, I knew.

393
00:33:23,585 --> 00:33:27,214
But I hoped you'd be plastic
that takes 100 years to rot.

394
00:33:27,339 --> 00:33:29,007
But I guess not.

395
00:33:29,133 --> 00:33:31,093
You really are a tin can bastard.

396
00:33:31,218 --> 00:33:34,930
A tin can bastard
that takes over 200 years to decompose.

397
00:33:35,514 --> 00:33:37,850
So what do you want me to do, huh?

398
00:33:38,392 --> 00:33:40,936
Who cares if I'm a tin can bastard?

399
00:33:41,061 --> 00:33:43,647
I'll just disappear from your life.

400
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:46,066
I said I'll get out of your life!

401
00:33:46,191 --> 00:33:47,568
What is your problem?

402
00:33:47,693 --> 00:33:51,238
I'm pissed because
you're even more pathetic than I thought.

403
00:33:54,700 --> 00:33:56,285
It pisses me off

404
00:33:56,410 --> 00:34:00,372
that I hurt the person I love the most
over a bastard like you.

405
00:34:00,497 --> 00:34:02,791
Damn it, what the hell?

406
00:34:02,916 --> 00:34:04,543
I'm a crazy bitch.

407
00:34:05,419 --> 00:34:08,756
I'm a crazy bitch
for having feelings for such a bastard.

408
00:34:54,343 --> 00:34:55,177
Lee Mi-do.

409
00:35:29,294 --> 00:35:31,672
Ms. Lee.

410
00:35:44,810 --> 00:35:45,727
Ms. Lee.

411
00:35:49,940 --> 00:35:52,109
Ms. Lee, can you hear me?

412
00:36:01,869 --> 00:36:03,203
What happened?

413
00:36:04,329 --> 00:36:05,581
You don't remember?

414
00:36:10,627 --> 00:36:11,712
There was a crash.

415
00:36:14,673 --> 00:36:17,009
-I'll get a doctor.
-No, I'm fine.

416
00:36:17,134 --> 00:36:18,719
No, you're not fine.

417
00:36:19,386 --> 00:36:21,597
I can be a bit impulsive.

418
00:36:22,639 --> 00:36:25,058
I'm sorry if I startled you.

419
00:36:27,936 --> 00:36:29,438
Your brother is coming.

420
00:36:31,064 --> 00:36:33,233
You need a guardian for the tests.

421
00:36:33,901 --> 00:36:36,862
He happened to call,
so I explained the situation.

422
00:36:37,946 --> 00:36:39,573
He should be here by now.

423
00:36:39,698 --> 00:36:40,699
Follow me.

424
00:36:41,825 --> 00:36:43,243
Hey, hold on a second.

425
00:36:43,368 --> 00:36:45,120
YUSEONG UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

426
00:36:45,245 --> 00:36:47,873
I didn't want to answer the phone either,

427
00:36:47,998 --> 00:36:51,501
but I hit you with my car,
so I'm the one at fault here.

428
00:36:51,627 --> 00:36:53,670
If I leave, it'd be a problem too.

429
00:36:53,795 --> 00:36:56,131
You're already a criminal anyway.

430
00:36:56,256 --> 00:36:59,009
What difference does it make
if you get one more charge?

431
00:36:59,134 --> 00:37:00,135
Excuse me?

432
00:37:01,094 --> 00:37:03,347
I'm hurt and tired, so just follow me.

433
00:37:03,472 --> 00:37:07,267
Okay. All right, I'll go.
I said I'm coming.

434
00:37:07,392 --> 00:37:09,311
You need to be careful right now.

435
00:37:10,437 --> 00:37:11,396
Does it hurt?

436
00:37:11,521 --> 00:37:14,524
Are you hurt anywhere else?

437
00:37:14,650 --> 00:37:16,109
What about you?

438
00:37:20,614 --> 00:37:22,074
Did you get hurt?

439
00:37:23,784 --> 00:37:25,953
You're can't even get injections.

440
00:37:26,078 --> 00:37:28,038
You're not hurt, are you?

441
00:37:34,086 --> 00:37:35,420
You bastard!

442
00:37:35,545 --> 00:37:36,755
Who the hell are you?

443
00:37:37,673 --> 00:37:39,257
Lee Mi-do, you okay? You hurt?

444
00:37:41,343 --> 00:37:43,971
I saw you grabbing Lee Mi-do, you bastard.

445
00:37:44,680 --> 00:37:45,555
Who are you?

446
00:37:45,681 --> 00:37:48,141
Laying your hands on her in a hospital?

447
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:49,518
Yeong-do!

448
00:37:50,185 --> 00:37:53,438
What are you doing? Let go of him!
What is this? Are you okay?

449
00:37:53,563 --> 00:37:55,148
Lee Mi-do! Who's this prick?!

450
00:37:55,273 --> 00:37:56,525
I said stop it!

451
00:37:56,650 --> 00:37:58,527
He was my junior in the army.

452
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:19,297
Are you okay?

453
00:38:21,299 --> 00:38:23,343
You're not hurt anywhere else, right?

454
00:38:28,515 --> 00:38:29,891
Lee Mi-do.

455
00:38:34,688 --> 00:38:36,148
You scared me.

456
00:38:39,401 --> 00:38:41,486
I feel like
you took ten years off my life.

457
00:39:10,557 --> 00:39:12,642
What is going on today?

458
00:39:13,685 --> 00:39:15,812
I think you're misunderstanding something.

459
00:39:17,564 --> 00:39:18,690
Ms. Lee and I

460
00:39:20,233 --> 00:39:21,610
aren't like that.

461
00:39:24,112 --> 00:39:26,698
I just liked her,
so I followed her around.

462
00:39:28,158 --> 00:39:29,785
But Ms. Lee wasn't interested.

463
00:39:31,787 --> 00:39:32,954
I mean it.

464
00:39:42,506 --> 00:39:43,882
Not buying it?

465
00:39:44,007 --> 00:39:46,843
You're just spouting nonsense.
You didn't even try to fool me.

466
00:39:50,055 --> 00:39:51,264
You caught me.

467
00:39:51,389 --> 00:39:53,475
Do you know what you did wrong?

468
00:39:54,434 --> 00:39:55,936
Too many things.

469
00:39:57,521 --> 00:39:58,855
What do you know?

470
00:40:00,273 --> 00:40:02,234
There's one thing I know for sure.

471
00:40:03,026 --> 00:40:05,695
Lee Mi-do got hurt,
and you're perfectly fine.

472
00:40:07,531 --> 00:40:10,075
What were you doing
while her arm got crushed?

473
00:40:10,826 --> 00:40:12,994
You couldn't even protect her!

474
00:40:16,123 --> 00:40:17,874
Stay away from Lee Mi-do.

475
00:40:19,459 --> 00:40:20,627
Or you'll regret it.

476
00:40:53,994 --> 00:40:55,453
I had my reasons.

477
00:40:58,206 --> 00:41:00,542
I know everything I say
will be an excuse, but--

478
00:41:00,667 --> 00:41:04,129
Just how miserable do you want to make me?

479
00:41:07,340 --> 00:41:09,593
Do you have any idea what you've done?

480
00:41:12,888 --> 00:41:16,224
You turned all our time together
into complete garbage.

481
00:41:18,560 --> 00:41:19,978
You had your reasons?

482
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:23,023
You had no other choice?

483
00:41:24,733 --> 00:41:26,776
You don't know why you did it either?

484
00:41:28,195 --> 00:41:29,696
Just be honest for once.

485
00:41:30,322 --> 00:41:32,532
You didn't give a damn about me,

486
00:41:33,366 --> 00:41:35,035
whether I'd get hurt or not

487
00:41:35,785 --> 00:41:38,079
or about tossing our time together
in the trash.

488
00:41:39,039 --> 00:41:41,875
You just selfishly did
whatever the hell you wanted.

489
00:41:50,842 --> 00:41:52,886
Is that really what you think?

490
00:41:56,097 --> 00:41:57,641
Do you really think…

491
00:42:00,268 --> 00:42:02,479
I didn't care if you got hurt

492
00:42:03,688 --> 00:42:05,982
or if our time together was ruined?

493
00:42:06,650 --> 00:42:08,860
That I ignored everything
and only thought of myself?

494
00:42:08,985 --> 00:42:12,113
-Am I wrong?
-Yes, you are.

495
00:42:13,490 --> 00:42:15,408
It was agonizing for me too.

496
00:42:18,328 --> 00:42:20,205
You mean everything to me, Namgung Ho.

497
00:42:21,373 --> 00:42:23,708
You're still so incredibly precious to me.

498
00:42:25,168 --> 00:42:28,713
I could never hurt you
after all you've been through.

499
00:42:28,838 --> 00:42:30,674
That made me hate myself even more.

500
00:42:31,258 --> 00:42:34,010
I tried so hard to hide it from you.
Actually…

501
00:42:34,135 --> 00:42:36,846
I fought so hard to hide it from myself.

502
00:42:36,972 --> 00:42:40,558
Do you know what everything you're saying
sounds like right now?

503
00:42:40,684 --> 00:42:43,228
"I liked him like crazy,
so I couldn't hold back."

504
00:42:43,353 --> 00:42:45,230
"You meant nothing." That's what I hear!

505
00:42:45,355 --> 00:42:46,356
Yeah!

506
00:42:46,481 --> 00:42:48,441
I liked him! He gave me butterflies!

507
00:42:55,532 --> 00:42:57,409
My daily life was always the same.

508
00:42:58,076 --> 00:43:00,287
Movies stopped being fun a long time ago.

509
00:43:01,288 --> 00:43:04,499
I had no hope for my future.
And I'm getting older.

510
00:43:05,500 --> 00:43:07,043
And so I thought,

511
00:43:07,794 --> 00:43:08,795
"Oh."

512
00:43:10,380 --> 00:43:13,425
"I'm just going
to slowly grow old like this."

513
00:43:20,265 --> 00:43:21,891
But my heart fluttered.

514
00:43:27,230 --> 00:43:31,234
If I say it felt like
he lit up my bleak, dark life,

515
00:43:32,819 --> 00:43:34,571
would you believe me?

516
00:43:44,456 --> 00:43:45,415
No.

517
00:43:49,794 --> 00:43:52,756
It's just a pathetic excuse to justify it.
Nothing more.

518
00:43:54,007 --> 00:43:56,468
Sugarcoating it must make you feel better.

519
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:02,640
For me…

520
00:44:06,644 --> 00:44:09,147
whenever you act like this,
it feels like a punishment.

521
00:44:11,483 --> 00:44:13,943
We never should have dated
in the first place.

522
00:44:15,445 --> 00:44:17,405
Before we ruin each other even more,

523
00:44:18,573 --> 00:44:20,658
let's get out of each other's lives.

524
00:45:09,249 --> 00:45:10,291
ALARM OFF

525
00:46:52,143 --> 00:46:54,729
What's this?
Did you see the notice just now?

526
00:46:54,854 --> 00:46:56,564
And palm oil is at 31%,

527
00:46:56,689 --> 00:47:00,026
powdered milk at 19%,
and raw sugar at 16%.

528
00:47:00,151 --> 00:47:02,445
Raw material prices are soaring.

529
00:47:02,570 --> 00:47:05,573
We need to prevent
further increases right now.

530
00:47:05,698 --> 00:47:07,742
Looking at the impact by product line,

531
00:47:07,867 --> 00:47:10,578
the chocolate line is highest at 11.4%.

532
00:47:10,703 --> 00:47:12,080
MANAGER EOM HO-SIK

533
00:47:16,125 --> 00:47:19,837
DISCIPLINARY NOTICE:
NAMGUNG HO, TF SNACK TEAM 3, ASST. MANAGER

534
00:47:19,963 --> 00:47:21,798
NAMGUNG HO IS HEREBY SUSPENDED
FOR ONE WEEK

535
00:47:21,923 --> 00:47:24,092
REASON: SUSPECTED OF RECEIVING BRIBES
FROM PARTNER COMPANY

536
00:47:27,136 --> 00:47:29,472
Namgung Ho? That Assistant Manager Gung?

537
00:47:29,597 --> 00:47:31,599
There are rumors
he's involved with loan sharks.

538
00:47:31,724 --> 00:47:33,309
He must have taken a bribe.

539
00:47:33,434 --> 00:47:35,144
Did he also rig

540
00:47:35,270 --> 00:47:37,397
that outsourcing rate with their CEO?

541
00:47:50,493 --> 00:47:52,287
KEEP YOUR 20-YEAR-OLD JOINTS HEALTHY
UNTIL YOU'RE 80. KNEE SLAP!

542
00:47:52,412 --> 00:47:54,497
By the Dongbo Pharma billboard.
There's a field and a ditch.

543
00:47:54,622 --> 00:47:56,207
You dumped them there, right?

544
00:48:07,635 --> 00:48:10,221
TO: ACE Q-LAB FOOD ANALYSIS INSTITUTE

545
00:48:21,983 --> 00:48:23,401
It's still slippery on the left.

546
00:48:24,861 --> 00:48:26,112
It's my fault.

547
00:48:28,114 --> 00:48:30,617
I put a GPS on Mr. Oh's truck last week.

548
00:48:30,742 --> 00:48:32,368
I think that's what went wrong.

549
00:48:34,412 --> 00:48:35,538
But the thing is,

550
00:48:36,623 --> 00:48:38,041
I was really careful.

551
00:48:38,833 --> 00:48:41,794
I used five VPNs to hide my identity,

552
00:48:41,919 --> 00:48:43,755
and I only paid with crypto.

553
00:48:44,714 --> 00:48:46,883
Even if the GPS was discovered…

554
00:48:51,304 --> 00:48:52,138
No way.

555
00:48:52,263 --> 00:48:53,473
Any sweet potatoes left?

556
00:48:53,598 --> 00:48:55,224
You couldn't have used them all.

557
00:48:56,017 --> 00:48:58,478
Mr. Namgung took them this morning.

558
00:49:02,649 --> 00:49:04,108
That's why you…

559
00:49:08,071 --> 00:49:09,739
It was a trap from the start.

560
00:49:10,782 --> 00:49:13,743
Bringing sweet potatoes
from the Cheonan Factory was a trap.

561
00:49:15,161 --> 00:49:17,038
The texture got too crunchy.

562
00:49:19,082 --> 00:49:20,917
I told them to make it denser.

563
00:49:21,042 --> 00:49:23,670
Man, the Frozen Dessert Department
is so lazy.

564
00:49:25,380 --> 00:49:26,673
You took them on purpose.

565
00:49:27,674 --> 00:49:28,591
Didn't you?

566
00:49:28,716 --> 00:49:30,927
You took them
knowing it was a trap, right?

567
00:49:32,679 --> 00:49:34,055
It's not that serious.

568
00:49:34,847 --> 00:49:36,265
At worst, the team disbands,

569
00:49:36,391 --> 00:49:39,227
I get a pay cut,
and I get sent to a factory.

570
00:49:39,977 --> 00:49:41,979
If I'm lucky,
a transfer to another department.

571
00:49:42,105 --> 00:49:44,816
You know why?
Because I'm completely clean.

572
00:49:46,776 --> 00:49:47,735
Park Su-a.

573
00:49:48,444 --> 00:49:50,363
Now is not the time to zone out.

574
00:49:50,488 --> 00:49:52,115
Pull yourself together.

575
00:49:52,824 --> 00:49:56,160
If they drop their guard thinking it's me,
you can investigate.

576
00:49:57,829 --> 00:50:00,331
And you need to investigate
and resolve this.

577
00:50:04,335 --> 00:50:06,504
So I can come back to the team.

578
00:50:06,629 --> 00:50:08,381
But this still isn't right.

579
00:50:08,506 --> 00:50:09,632
I'll talk to them.

580
00:50:09,757 --> 00:50:11,968
Then this gets buried forever.

581
00:50:15,096 --> 00:50:17,265
I'm not going to look into it.

582
00:50:22,186 --> 00:50:23,396
So you do it.

583
00:50:25,440 --> 00:50:27,233
You're the only one who can.

584
00:50:29,986 --> 00:50:31,738
Why the sudden change?

585
00:50:31,863 --> 00:50:33,740
You didn't want me doing this.

586
00:50:35,950 --> 00:50:37,285
That was a lie.

587
00:50:39,120 --> 00:50:41,581
I thought you were really cool
for doing it.

588
00:50:43,750 --> 00:50:45,501
I thought you were amazing.

589
00:50:48,546 --> 00:50:49,964
So you should keep going.

590
00:50:51,090 --> 00:50:52,175
Doing what's cool.

591
00:51:18,785 --> 00:51:19,994
Mr. Namgung.

592
00:51:20,870 --> 00:51:22,371
Your phone keeps ringing…

593
00:51:25,374 --> 00:51:26,459
45 MISSED CALLS FROM YEONG-DO

594
00:51:27,627 --> 00:51:30,171
I checked just in case.
I wasn't snooping or anything.

595
00:51:30,963 --> 00:51:31,881
YEONG-DO

596
00:51:33,299 --> 00:51:34,175
What is this?

597
00:51:34,300 --> 00:51:37,220
Namgung, did you know about this too?

598
00:51:37,386 --> 00:51:39,597
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO
QUITS FILM STARRING SONG HAE-NA

599
00:51:39,722 --> 00:51:41,557
REPLACED BY DIRECTOR NA SEUNG-HO

600
00:51:46,938 --> 00:51:48,606
The person you're trying to reach is…

601
00:51:51,567 --> 00:51:53,236
Still no word from Lee Mi-do?

602
00:51:53,361 --> 00:51:55,822
Her phone is off. What do we do?

603
00:51:56,989 --> 00:52:00,201
She always hides when there's trouble.
Every freaking time.

604
00:52:00,952 --> 00:52:03,329
How many times did I say she'd fail?

605
00:52:03,454 --> 00:52:06,457
She should have quit
when her film tanked five years ago.

606
00:52:07,208 --> 00:52:08,501
This time, no matter what,

607
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:11,212
I'm going to make that brat
quit directing for good.

608
00:52:11,337 --> 00:52:12,922
She'd be better off doing hair.

609
00:52:13,047 --> 00:52:15,091
Why did she even try to make movies?

610
00:52:15,967 --> 00:52:16,801
Yeong-do.

611
00:52:16,926 --> 00:52:18,928
Yeah, I'm sorry. I really am.

612
00:52:19,053 --> 00:52:20,596
I can barely look at you.

613
00:52:20,721 --> 00:52:22,181
When Lee Mi-do gets back here,

614
00:52:22,306 --> 00:52:26,102
I'm going to chew her out
for losing her mind and wasting her youth.

615
00:52:26,227 --> 00:52:28,020
I'll whip that brat into shape.

616
00:52:28,145 --> 00:52:29,146
Shut your mouth.

617
00:52:33,359 --> 00:52:36,195
If you ever talk like that
in front of Lee Mi-do,

618
00:52:37,780 --> 00:52:39,407
I won't let it slide.

619
00:52:40,157 --> 00:52:41,409
We're done.

620
00:52:45,413 --> 00:52:47,874
Lee Mi-do is the one hurting the most.

621
00:52:47,999 --> 00:52:49,500
What do you even know?

622
00:52:53,462 --> 00:52:54,547
Ho.

623
00:53:01,929 --> 00:53:02,805
Ms. Ma.

624
00:53:03,389 --> 00:53:06,267
I know you're very disappointed in Mi-do.

625
00:53:08,811 --> 00:53:10,563
But she really did her best.

626
00:53:12,481 --> 00:53:16,569
If you see her,
please just pretend this didn't happen.

627
00:53:17,153 --> 00:53:18,613
Or she'll fall apart.

628
00:53:21,324 --> 00:53:22,825
Please.

629
00:53:33,419 --> 00:53:34,921
I'll call when I find Mi-do.

630
00:54:04,742 --> 00:54:05,576
Welcome.

631
00:54:15,252 --> 00:54:16,128
MIDORI

632
00:54:18,714 --> 00:54:21,842
The person you're trying to reach
is unavailable. At the tone…

633
00:54:35,731 --> 00:54:37,858
Stay away from Lee Mi-do.

634
00:54:37,984 --> 00:54:39,151
Or you'll regret it.

635
00:54:40,027 --> 00:54:41,404
And what about you?

636
00:54:44,573 --> 00:54:46,033
What did you do for her?

637
00:54:49,412 --> 00:54:51,872
You have no idea
why she had that accident.

638
00:54:53,457 --> 00:54:55,751
You wouldn't talk like that if you knew.

639
00:54:57,086 --> 00:54:59,213
Watch your damn mouth.

640
00:54:59,338 --> 00:55:01,132
My patience has limits.

641
00:55:04,552 --> 00:55:06,137
You really don't know.

642
00:55:08,889 --> 00:55:11,350
Do you think
it's just Lee Mi-do's arm that's broken?

643
00:55:13,352 --> 00:55:14,311
It's not just that.

644
00:55:15,021 --> 00:55:17,314
She's far more broken inside.

645
00:55:28,451 --> 00:55:30,286
We got the dashcam footage

646
00:55:30,411 --> 00:55:33,122
from the car that hit Han Tae-seung.

647
00:55:33,247 --> 00:55:34,874
It's a bit sensitive,

648
00:55:35,666 --> 00:55:37,376
but please check the video first.

649
00:56:32,765 --> 00:56:35,267
YEONHWARU

650
00:56:35,559 --> 00:56:37,228
When did it start?

651
00:56:38,104 --> 00:56:40,523
When did Lee Mi-do
start to slowly wither away?

652
00:56:41,690 --> 00:56:43,025
Namgung.

653
00:56:43,692 --> 00:56:46,112
Is it really okay if my movie flops?

654
00:56:46,862 --> 00:56:50,366
You said you didn't care if it flopped.

655
00:56:51,617 --> 00:56:53,202
I'm terrible, aren't I?

656
00:56:55,079 --> 00:56:56,497
You must be disappointed.

657
00:57:02,378 --> 00:57:03,754
Lee Mi-do was…

658
00:57:07,174 --> 00:57:11,095
the brightest person I ever knew.

659
00:57:31,240 --> 00:57:35,828
She was always the main character.

660
00:57:35,953 --> 00:57:39,540
In recognition of outstanding achievement
at the Seoul Youth Film Festival,

661
00:57:39,665 --> 00:57:41,458
hosted by the Garam Foundation,

662
00:57:41,584 --> 00:57:43,210
we hereby present this award.

663
00:57:49,008 --> 00:57:52,469
2009 YOUTH FILM FESTIVAL GRAND PRIZE
LEE MI-DO, YEONUL HIGH SCHOOL

664
00:58:07,276 --> 00:58:11,155
Everyone loved you.

665
00:58:23,792 --> 00:58:25,878
Your dreams

666
00:58:26,003 --> 00:58:27,630
gave me butterflies,

667
00:58:28,339 --> 00:58:29,423
and I couldn't help

668
00:58:30,174 --> 00:58:32,468
but love you for it.

669
00:59:04,667 --> 00:59:06,919
YEONUL ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

670
00:59:38,367 --> 00:59:39,743
You know…

671
00:59:41,370 --> 00:59:42,955
when I was young…

672
00:59:45,291 --> 00:59:47,793
I never once imagined…

673
00:59:49,670 --> 00:59:52,006
that I'd grow into a pathetic adult.

674
00:59:54,800 --> 00:59:56,051
I was crazy.

675
00:59:57,344 --> 00:59:58,804
So young and arrogant.

676
01:00:02,516 --> 01:00:04,518
But what's more humiliating…

677
01:00:06,395 --> 01:00:08,981
is showing you this side of me.

678
01:00:10,816 --> 01:00:14,528
I only ever wanted
to show you my best side.

679
01:00:16,322 --> 01:00:18,991
But I always show you my worst side.

680
01:00:21,744 --> 01:00:23,162
I hate that.

681
01:00:51,982 --> 01:00:53,442
Your hands are so cold.

682
01:00:55,861 --> 01:00:57,446
Let's go home, Mi-do.

683
01:01:12,336 --> 01:01:14,380
Don't you hate me?

684
01:01:17,174 --> 01:01:19,301
Even after how I treated you.

685
01:01:20,886 --> 01:01:22,137
Why don't you…

686
01:01:23,764 --> 01:01:24,723
Why…

687
01:01:28,560 --> 01:01:29,603
Mi-do.

688
01:01:33,565 --> 01:01:35,984
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

689
01:01:38,237 --> 01:01:39,947
I haven't lost my mind,

690
01:01:41,615 --> 01:01:43,700
and I'm completely serious.

691
01:01:54,044 --> 01:01:55,421
Go see that guy.

692
01:02:01,343 --> 01:02:02,428
That guy…

693
01:02:06,181 --> 01:02:08,100
who lit up your bleak, dark life.

694
01:02:12,938 --> 01:02:14,189
Go see him.

695
01:02:54,938 --> 01:02:56,815
THANK YOU TO UM HYO-SUP
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

696
01:02:57,649 --> 01:02:59,610
Put him on an anchovy fishing boat,
he's fine.

697
01:02:59,735 --> 01:03:00,652
He's relentless.

698
01:03:00,777 --> 01:03:02,696
Go get some mudflat samples.

699
01:03:02,821 --> 01:03:05,407
You know that Su-a has feelings for you.

700
01:03:05,532 --> 01:03:08,827
Should I let you drag me along,
worrying that you'll dump me?

701
01:03:08,952 --> 01:03:11,205
You should've flat-out denied it.

702
01:03:11,330 --> 01:03:13,999
I would've just looked the other way!

703
01:03:14,124 --> 01:03:15,375
There's nothing between him and me.

704
01:03:16,293 --> 01:03:18,378
He doesn't even know I like him.

705
01:03:18,504 --> 01:03:20,339
Then you do it, too.

706
01:03:20,464 --> 01:03:22,299
You see other women, too.

707
01:03:23,634 --> 01:03:25,594
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
